<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia sets Jun Tapis price at $20.11 down $1.19.</title>
<headline>Malaysia sets Jun Tapis price at $20.11 down $1.19.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's state-owned Petronas has reduced the June term lifting price of its Tapis crude to $20.11 per barrel, from $21.30 in May, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Petronas also set the July premium for Tapis at 15 cents per barrel, lower than the 30 cents premium set for June.  </p>
<p>June Labuan was set at a fixed differential of Tapis plus 15 cents and Miri was set at Tapis plus 10 cents -- unchanged from the previous month.</p>
<p>Bintulu differential was set at Tapis less 40 cents, also unchanged.</p>
<p>The price of June Dulang crude was set at $19.29 from $20.41 in May.</p>
